 "_about": "IMSLP scoring-category names (the parts of 'For 2 violins, viola, cello') mapped to lib/chamber/vocab.ts InstrumentKey. A value is an InstrumentKey; an object when one name is several players ('piano 4 hands'; an object is the whole part, so the count before '2 pianos 8 hands' is not multiplied); or '!reason' when the name puts a scoring outside the section or the vocabulary has no key for it. Plurals ('violins', 'double basses') are found through their singular; a plural without a count ('voices', 'viols') means an unspecified number and puts the scoring out. scripts/chamber/imslp_census.ts fails on any name that is not here. The glass harmonica (Mozart's K. 617 and K. 356) is mapped to celesta, today's usual substitute; the work's notes name the glass harmonica (owner, 2026-10-16: a note, not a new instrument).",
